STARTFONT 2.1
COMMENT Strike 1 of a Newton 'sfnt' font (bloc/bdat): tools/fonts/newtonsfnt.py,
COMMENT tools/fonts/README.md.  The builder reads the BLOC_* properties and the
COMMENT glyphs - STARTCHAR gN (N the glyph id; otherwise ENCODING through 'cmap'),
COMMENT DWIDTH (the advance), BBX (width, height, the bearing x, the bottom row's
COMMENT y: bearing y less the height) and the BITMAP rows.  A glyph id in the
COMMENT subtable ranges with no glyph here has no image (the missing glyph is 0).
COMMENT The other properties, SIZE, FONTBOUNDINGBOX and SWIDTH are worked out and
COMMENT not read back: change BLOC_HORI_* (the line metrics the ROM draws text by)
COMMENT to match an edit that changes the strike's extent.
FONT -Apple-Roman Regular-Medium-R-Normal--10-100-72-72-P-0-Apple-Roman
SIZE 10 72 72
FONTBOUNDINGBOX 13 12 -1 -2
STARTPROPERTIES 37
FONT_ASCENT 10
FONT_DESCENT 2
PIXEL_SIZE 10
FAMILY_NAME "Roman Regular"
BLOC_COLOR_REF 0
BLOC_HORI_ASCENDER 10
BLOC_HORI_DESCENDER -2
BLOC_HORI_WIDTH_MAX 13
BLOC_HORI_CARET_SLOPE_NUMERATOR 0
BLOC_HORI_CARET_SLOPE_DENOMINATOR 1
BLOC_HORI_CARET_OFFSET 0
BLOC_HORI_MIN_ORIGIN_SB -1
BLOC_HORI_MIN_ADVANCE_SB -1
BLOC_HORI_MAX_BEFORE_BL 10
BLOC_HORI_MIN_AFTER_BL -2
BLOC_HORI_PAD1 0
BLOC_HORI_PAD2 0
BLOC_VERT_ASCENDER 0
BLOC_VERT_DESCENDER 0
BLOC_VERT_WIDTH_MAX 12
BLOC_VERT_CARET_SLOPE_NUMERATOR 0
BLOC_VERT_CARET_SLOPE_DENOMINATOR 1
BLOC_VERT_CARET_OFFSET 0
BLOC_VERT_MIN_ORIGIN_SB 119
BLOC_VERT_MIN_ADVANCE_SB -120
BLOC_VERT_MAX_BEFORE_BL 0
BLOC_VERT_MIN_AFTER_BL 92
BLOC_VERT_PAD1 0
BLOC_VERT_PAD2 0
BLOC_START_GLYPH 0
BLOC_END_GLYPH 257
BLOC_PPEM_X 10
BLOC_PPEM_Y 10
BLOC_BIT_DEPTH 1
BLOC_FLAGS 1
BLOC_INDEX_SUBTABLES 1
BLOC_INDEX_SUBTABLE_0 "0 257 3 1 0"
